You can create a custom WordPress block with a heading, paragraph, and image by following these steps:

1. Create a new PHP file in the `wp-content/plugins` directory of your WordPress installation. For example, `custom-block.php`.
2. In this file, add the following code to define the block:
```php
<?php
/**
 * Custom Block Plugin
 *
 * @package Custom Block
 */

// Hook into the WordPress block editor
function register_custom_block() {
    // Register the block
    register_block_type( 'custom-block/block' );
}
add_action( 'init', 'register_custom_block' );
```
3. Create a new directory in the `wp-content/plugins` directory called `custom-block`. Inside this directory, create a new file called `block.json`. This file will define the block's metadata.
```json
{
  "name": "Custom Block",
  "title": "Custom Block",
  "description": "A custom block with a heading, paragraph, and image",
  "icon": "format-image",
  "category": "common",
  "keywords": ["custom", "block", "heading", "paragraph", "image"]
}
```
4. Create a new file in the `wp-content/plugins/custom-block` directory called `editor.js`. This file will define the block's editor functionality.
```javascript
import { registerBlockType } from '@wordpress/blocks';
import { InspectorControls } from '@wordpress/block-editor';

registerBlockType( 'custom-block/block', {
  title: 'Custom Block',
  icon: 'format-image',
  category: 'common',
  edit: Edit,
  save: Save,
} );

function Edit( { attributes, setAttributes } ) {
  const { heading, paragraph, image } = attributes;

  return (
    <div>
      <h2>{ heading }</h2>
      <p>{ paragraph }</p>
      <img src={ image } />
    </div>
  );
}

function Save( { attributes } ) {
  const { heading, paragraph, image } = attributes;

  return (
    <div>
      <h2>{ heading }</h2>
      <p>{ paragraph }</p>
      <img src={ image } />
    </div>
  );
}
```
5. Create a new file in the `wp-content/plugins/custom-block` directory called `style.css`. This file will define the block's styles.
```css
.custom-block {
  padding: 20px;
  border: 1px solid #ccc;
  border-radius: 10px;
  box-shadow: 0 0 10px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.1);
}

.custom-block h2 {
  font-size: 24px;
  font-weight: bold;
  margin-bottom: 10px;
}

.custom-block p {
  font-size: 18px;
  margin-bottom: 20px;
}

.custom-block img {
  width: 100%;
  height: 200px;
  object-fit: cover;
  border-radius: 10px;
}
```
6. Activate the plugin by going to the WordPress admin dashboard and clicking on the "Plugins" menu. Find the "Custom Block" plugin and click the "Activate" link.

7. Go to the WordPress block editor and click on the "+" icon to add a new block. Search for "Custom Block" and click on it to add it to the editor.

8. In the block editor, you can now add a heading, paragraph, and image to the block by clicking on the corresponding fields.

That's it! You have now created a custom WordPress block with a heading, paragraph, and image.

